<header><p class="st-kicker">theocracy · Scandinavia and the Baltic</p><h1 class="st-title">Livonian Brothers of the Sword</h1><p class="st-meta">1202 CE – 1237 CE · capital Wenden</p></header>
<p class="st-teaser">Crusading military order founded in Riga in 1202, which conquered Livonia and Estonia before being destroyed at Saule in 1236.</p>
<div class="st-body"><div class="st-text"><h2>Origins</h2><p><a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/albert-of-riga">Bishop Albert of Riga</a> and the Cistercian <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/theoderich-von-treyden">Theoderich</a> founded the Brothers of the Sword in 1202 to provide a permanent army for the Livonian <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/crusade">crusade</a>, modelled on the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/knights-templar">Templars</a>. <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/pope-innocent-iii">Pope Innocent III</a> approved it in 1204, and its knights wore a white mantle with a red sword and cross.</p><h2>Rule and society</h2><p>The Order's knight-brothers, mostly from <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/saxony">Saxony</a> and <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/westphalia">Westphalia</a>, lived under a monastic rule and governed conquered land from castles such as <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/cesis">Wenden</a> (Cēsis) and <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/viljandi">Fellin</a>. The <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/bishop">bishop</a> granted them a third of conquered territory. Under masters <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/wenno">Wenno</a> and <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/volquin">Volquin</a> they subdued the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/livonians">Livs</a>, <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/latgalians">Latgalians</a> and <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/estonians">Estonians</a>, often quarrelling with the bishops and with <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/denmark">Denmark</a> over the spoils.</p><h2>Decline and legacy</h2><p>In 1236 a <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/crusade">crusade</a> against <a class="enc-link st-link" href="/empire/grand-duchy-of-lithuania">Lithuania</a> ended in disaster at the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/battle-of-saule">Battle of Saule</a>, where <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/samogitians">Samogitians</a> and <a class="enc-link st-link" href="/state/semigallians">Semigallians</a> killed Master <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/volquin">Volquin</a> and about fifty brothers. The survivors were incorporated in 1237 into the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/teutonic-order">Teutonic Order</a> as its Livonian branch, the <a class="enc-link st-link" href="/state/livonian-order">Livonian Order</a>.</p></div><aside class="st-side"><figure class="st-fig"><img src="/images/states/livonian-brothers-of-the-sword.jpg" alt="Livonian Brothers of the Sword" width="320" height="251"><figcaption>Image: Dirk Jansz van Santen · Public domain · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Atlas_Van_der_Hagen-KW1049B10_029-LIVONIA_Vulgo_Lyetland.jpeg" target="_blank" rel="noopener">source</a></figcaption></figure><dl class="st-facts"><dt>Years</dt><dd>1202 CE – 1237 CE</dd><dt>Century</dt><dd><a href="/centuries/13th-century">13th century</a></dd><dt>Type</dt><dd>theocracy</dd><dt>Character</dt><dd>theocratic</dd><dt>Capital</dt><dd>Wenden</dd><dt>Rulers</dt><dd>Wenno, Volquin</dd><dt>Religion</dt><dd>Catholic Christianity</dd><dt>Language</dt><dd>Middle Low German, Latin</dd><dt>Today</dt><dd><a href="/countries/latvia">Latvia</a>, <a href="/countries/estonia">Estonia</a></dd><dt>Also</dt><dd>Order of the Sword Brothers, Fratres militiae Christi Livoniae, Schwertbrüderorden</dd></dl><figure class="st-locator"><a href="/atlas?year=1220&amp;focus=livonian-brothers-of-the-sword" aria-label="Livonian Brothers of the Sword on the atlas"><svg class="map map-loc" viewBox="5234 250 640 512" role="img" aria-label="Map: where Livonian Brothers of the Sword lay"><image href="/maps/world.svg" x="0" y="0" width="10000" height="4393"/><path class="map-dot-n" d="M5568 520h0M5550 509h0M5520 501h0M5554 512h0M5546 487h0M5478 463h0M5513 441h0M5541 451h0M5540 452h0M5546 457h0"/><path class="map-dot-halo" d="M5554 506h0"/><path class="map-dot-ap" d="M5554 506h0"/></svg></a><figcaption